INT. MARITIME ARCHIVE - TIDE-TABLE ROOM - DAY

Floor-to-ceiling shelves of cloth-bound almanacs. A reading ladder on rails. A long oak table under a green-shaded lamp. Rain on skylights.

DETECTIVE SOLEDAD MARQUEZ-OYELARAN (40s, blazer, notebook) sits at the table with three almanacs open before her. At the far end, the ARCHIVIST, AUGUSTINE FEATHERSTONE (60s, bow tie, cotton gloves), shelves a volume on the ladder.

SOLEDAD
Mr. Featherstone, you said the logs for June are missing.

AUGUSTINE
Not missing. Misfiled.

SOLEDAD
Which is different how?

AUGUSTINE
Misfiled means they exist, but where they ought to be, they are not.

She lifts a volume. Flips a page. Puts it down. Her eyes track a column of numbers.

SOLEDAD
These tides don't match the harbor master's report.

AUGUSTINE
They wouldn't. Harbor masters report what they hope.

She laughs, once, short. He climbs down the ladder, one rung at a time. She stands. They both reach for the same almanac on the table; her hand covers his. They stop.

SOLEDAD
Sorry.

AUGUSTINE
Quite all right.

They each pull back an inch. He dusts the cover with his glove. She turns the book to face him.

SOLEDAD
June the ninth. High water at 3:12. Yet the dock log has her ship leaving at 2:50.

AUGUSTINE
She'd have grounded on the bar.

SOLEDAD
Unless she didn't leave at 2:50.

AUGUSTINE
Or the log is wrong.

SOLEDAD
Or somebody wants it to be.

A long pause. Rain. He removes his gloves, folds them, lays them on the table. She watches his hands.

AUGUSTINE
Detective, I've kept these tables for thirty-four years. Not once has a number been altered.

SOLEDAD
Not by you.

AUGUSTINE
Not by me.

SOLEDAD
Then by whom?

He crosses to a shelf and takes down a slim volume with a black spine. He carries it to her and lays it open to a page where one entry has been scraped away and rewritten in a different ink.

AUGUSTINE
Her.

SOLEDAD
Who?

AUGUSTINE
The previous archivist. She left in July.

Soledad reads the entry. Then looks at him, and he at her, both of them leaning over the page, and neither of them moves for a long moment.
